<%# The signing wait.

    This used to be a pulsing icon, the sentence "Approve the signing request in
    your Nostr signer app", and a percentage bar — for up to 120 seconds. It
    never said how long is normal, which of the user's identities was being
    asked, how many approvals were coming, or that the tab could be closed. The
    count existed in the code (total_items) and was used only to divide a
    percentage, so people tapped once and walked away mid-queue.

    The media upload path already did this better — "Approve the upload in your
    signer app (1 of 2)…" — so the flow the product exists for was the worst one
    in it.

    Now: one row per event, each naming the identity it is asking for, with
    elapsed time against a stated expectation, and four distinct failure causes
    instead of one sentence covering all of them. %>
<div id="signing-progress">
  <% reposts = post.reposts.includes(:account).to_a %>
  <% signed_count = (post.signed_event.present? ? 1 : 0) + reposts.count { |r| r.signed_event.present? } %>
  <% total_events = reposts.size + 1 %>

  <% if post.scheduled? || post.published? %>
    <div class="border rule px-4 py-3.5">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <%= lamp(:on) %>
        <p class="eng">Locked &middot; <%= pluralize(total_events, "event") %> signed</p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
        Signed and held. Nothing else is needed from you — it publishes at its
        scheduled time on its own.
      </p>
    </div>

  <% elsif local_assigns[:failed] || (post.failed? && post.signed_event.blank? && post.unsigned_event.present?) %>
    <div class="alarm is-stacked" role="alert">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
        <%= lamp(:alarm) %>
        <p class="eng text-red-700 dark:text-red-300">Not signed</p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-red-800 dark:text-red-200">
        <%= local_assigns[:error] || "Your signer did not return a signature." %>
      </p>

      <%# Four causes the codebase actually distinguishes, instead of one
          sentence that covers all of them and helps with none. %>
      <details class="mt-3">
        <summary class="eng cursor-pointer text-red-700 dark:text-red-300">Why this happens</summary>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-red-800 dark:text-red-200">
          <li><strong>You did not approve it in time.</strong> Amber gives you about two minutes. Retry and keep the phone in hand.</li>
          <li><strong>You denied it.</strong> Retry sends a fresh request.</li>
          <li><strong>The signer relay was unreachable.</strong> <%= post.account.signer_relay.presence || "The relay this account pairs through" %> may be rate-limiting or down; relay.damus.io in particular throttles NIP-46 traffic.</li>
          <li>
            <strong>The pairing predates this permission.</strong>
            <%= link_to "Re-pair #{post.account.display_name_or_npub}", re_pair_account_path(post.account),
                  class: "underline underline-offset-2" %> — it keeps the account's posts and settings.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </details>

      <div class="mt-3.5">
        <%= button_to "Ask again", retry_sign_post_path(post), method: :post,
              class: "condensed border border-amber-500 bg-amber-500 px-3.5 py-2 text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-[#1a1714] hover:bg-amber-400" %>
      </div>
    </div>

  <% elsif post.awaiting_signature? %>
    <div class="border border-amber-500 bg-amber-500/6 px-4 py-3.5"
         data-controller="elapsed" data-elapsed-start-value="<%= post.updated_at.iso8601 %>"
         role="status" aria-live="polite">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
          <%= lamp(:wait) %>
          <p class="eng text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400">
            Approve in Amber &middot; <%= signed_count %> of <%= total_events %> done
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="font-mono text-[13px] font-bold tabular text-amber-700 dark:text-amber-400"
           data-elapsed-target="readout" aria-label="Time elapsed">00:00</p>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-2.5 max-w-prose text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200">
        <% if total_events > 1 %>
          <strong><%= total_events %> separate approvals</strong> are queued — one for the post and
          one for each repost. Amber asks for them in turn.
        <% else %>
          One approval is queued, for the post itself.
        <% end %>
        Usually under 30 seconds; Amber allows about two minutes per request.
        <strong>You can close this tab</strong> — signing continues in the background.
      </p>

      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-red-700 dark:text-red-400" data-elapsed-target="note" hidden>
        Past two minutes. Amber has probably stopped waiting — check your phone, then ask again.
      </p>

      <%# The queue itself. Each row names the identity being asked for, because
          with nineteen paired accounts "approve the signing request" does not
          say whose key is on the screen. %>
      <ul class="mt-3.5 border-t border-amber-500/30">
        <li class="flex items-center gap-3 border-b border-amber-500/20 py-2">
          <%= lamp(post.signed_event.present? ? :on : :wait) %>
          <span class="eng w-14">1 of <%= total_events %></span>
          <%= identity(post.account) %>
          <span class="ml-auto eng"><%= post.signed_event.present? ? "Locked" : "Asking" %></span>
        </li>
        <% reposts.each_with_index do |repost, i| %>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3 border-b border-amber-500/20 py-2">
            <%= lamp(repost.signed_event.present? ? :on : :off) %>
            <span class="eng w-14"><%= i + 2 %> of <%= total_events %></span>
            <%= identity(repost.account) %>
            <span class="ml-auto eng"><%= repost.signed_event.present? ? "Locked" : "Queued" %></span>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
